Job 1 — Python: From Blocks to Thinking
1. Introduction

Python is a high-level, text-based programming language used to give instructions to computers. Before writing Python code, it is important to learn how to think logically and arrange instructions in the correct order.
For a Production Engineer, programming can help with:
Analysing production and cycle-time data
Managing quality records
Performing calculations
Automating repetitive tasks


2. Algorithm

An algorithm is a finite, step-by-step procedure used to solve a problem or perform a task.
Example: Manufacturing Process

Raw Material
     ↓
Cutting
     ↓
Drilling
     ↓
Finishing
     ↓
Inspection
     ↓
Finished Part

Characteristics of an Algorithm
Clear – each step is understandable.
Ordered – steps follow a logical sequence.
Finite – it eventually ends.
Unambiguous – each step has one clear meaning.
Effective – it should solve the intended problem.
An algorithm is like a recipe for solving a problem.


3. Sequence

A sequence is a set of instructions performed in a particular order.
Example: Making Tea

Add tea leaves & spices
        ↓
Boil water
        ↓
Add milk & sugar
        ↓
Simmer
        ↓
Strain into cup
        ↓
Serve

If the order is changed, the final result may also change.
Programming works in the same way: instructions are executed according to their sequence.


